{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Brings.BringUTContactChirality","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Brings.BringUTContactChirality","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Brings.BringConeLinkEulerNumber"],"declarations":24,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.canonicalResidue_chiral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.canonicalResidue_chiral","kind":"theorem","line":317,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringUTContactChirality.lean#L317-L318","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.canonicalResidue_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.canonicalResidue_eq","kind":"theorem","line":314,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringUTContactChirality.lean#L314-L315","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.canonicalResidue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.canonicalResidue","kind":"def","line":311,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringUTContactChirality.lean#L311-L312","doc":"The canonical fibre linking residue under the 2026-10-12 geodesic ruling: `−1/6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.unit_speed_alpha","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.unit_speed_alpha","kind":"theorem","line":295,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringUTContactChirality.lean#L295-L300","doc":"**Unit speed is preserved**: `α(X + κV) = 1`, so every strand stays positively transverse. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.geodesic_curvature_eq_eta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.geodesic_curvature_eq_eta","kind":"theorem","line":290,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringUTContactChirality.lean#L290-L293","doc":"**The connection form is the geodesic curvature**: `η(X + κV) = κ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.geodesic_residue_chiral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.geodesic_residue_chiral","kind":"theorem","line":261,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringUTContactChirality.lean#L261-L268","doc":"**The geodesic residue is chiral too**: `−1/6 ≢ 1/6 (mod 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.geodesic_residue_eq_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.geodesic_residue_eq_neg","kind":"theorem","line":256,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringUTContactChirality.lean#L256-L259","doc":"**Geodesic reading**: the orientation is reversed, so `e = +6` and the residue is `−1/6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.fibre_linking_residue_chiral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.fibre_linking_residue_chiral","kind":"theorem","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringUTContactChirality.lean#L226-L234","doc":"**The residue is chiral**: `1/6` and its orientation-reverse `−1/6` differ by a\nnon-integer, so they are different elements of `ℚ/ℤ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.bring_fibre_linking_residue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.bring_fibre_linking_residue","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringUTContactChirality.lean#L223-L224","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.fibreLinkingResidue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.fibreLinkingResidue","kind":"def","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringUTContactChirality.lean#L220-L221","doc":"The torsion linking residue of the fibre class: `−1/e`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.fibre_positively_transverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.fibre_positively_transverse","kind":"theorem","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringUTContactChirality.lean#L217-L218","doc":"**Fibre strands are positively transverse**: `η(∂_θ) = 1 > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.eta_volume_neg_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.eta_volume_neg_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringUTContactChirality.lean#L213-L215","doc":"**The orientation does not depend on the fibre direction**: `(−η) ∧ d(−η) = η ∧ dη`\n(each factor changes sign). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.legendrian_duality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.legendrian_duality","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringUTContactChirality.lean#L179-L185","doc":"**Legendrian duality**: the geodesic spray is `η`-horizontal and the fibre is `α`-horizontal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.contact_orientations_opposite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.contact_orientations_opposite","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringUTContactChirality.lean#L173-L177","doc":"**The two canonical contact forms orient `UT(Σ)` oppositely.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.fibre_contact_volume_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.fibre_contact_volume_coeff","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringUTContactChirality.lean#L167-L171","doc":"**`η ∧ dη = +1/y²`.** With `η = (1/y, 0, 1)`, `dη_{xy} = ∂ₓη_y − ∂_yη_x = 1/y²` and\n`dη_{xθ} = dη_{yθ} = 0`, the coefficient `η_x dη_{yθ} − η_y dη_{xθ} + η_θ dη_{xy}` is `1/y²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.reeb_positively_transverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.reeb_positively_transverse","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringUTContactChirality.lean#L146-L149","doc":"**Reeb strands are positively transverse**: `α(R) > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.reeb_contraction_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.reeb_contraction_zero","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringUTContactChirality.lean#L139-L144","doc":"**`ι_R dα = 0`**: the three components `Σᵢ Rⁱ dα_{ij}` vanish. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.reeb_alpha_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.reeb_alpha_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringUTContactChirality.lean#L132-L137","doc":"**`α(R) = 1`** for the geodesic spray `R = (y cos θ, y sin θ, −cos θ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.bring_link_chiral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.bring_link_chiral","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringUTContactChirality.lean#L103-L106","doc":"**`UT(Σ₄)` is chiral**: Euler number `−6`, so `e ≠ −e`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.euler_chiral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.euler_chiral","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringUTContactChirality.lean#L98-L101","doc":"**Orientation reversal negates the Euler number; a nonzero Euler number forbids a\nfibre-preserving orientation reversal.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.iota_lift_det","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.iota_lift_det","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringUTContactChirality.lean#L95-L96","doc":"The lift `(x, y, θ) ↦ (−x, y, π − θ)` has Jacobian `diag(−1, 1, −1)`, determinant `+1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.iota_pullback_alpha","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.iota_pullback_alpha","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringUTContactChirality.lean#L87-L93","doc":"**Conjugation preserves `α`.** Under `(x, y, θ) ↦ (−x, y, π − θ)`, the `dx` coefficient\n`cos θ / y` pulls back to `cos (π − θ)·(−1)/y` and the `dy` coefficient `sin θ / y` to\n`sin (π − θ)/y`; both are unchanged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.contact_volume_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.contact_volume_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringUTContactChirality.lean#L82-L85","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.contact_volume_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.UTContactChirality.contact_volume_coeff","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/BringUTContactChirality.lean#L72-L80","doc":"**`α ∧ dα` is nowhere zero.** With `α = (cos θ dx + sin θ dy)/y`, the coefficient of\n`dx ∧ dy ∧ dθ` in `α ∧ dα` is `a_x·(∂_y a_θ − ∂_θ a_y) − a_y·(∂_x a_θ − ∂_θ a_x)`, with\n`∂_θ a_y = cos θ / y`, `∂_θ a_x = −sin θ / y` and `a_θ = 0`; it equals `−1/y²`. (The partial\nderivatives are entered by hand; `ut_contact_orientation_probe.py` checks them symbolically.) ","signatureChunk":0}]}